 <p>Or98a makes the difference concrete: median GREEN-positive area is 97.55%, but only 2/286 eligible objects (0.70%) exceed the local GREEN threshold; RED area is 23.61% versus 2/286 objects (0.70%). RED object positivity changes from 30.77% at P95 to 0.70% at P99. Broad fluorescence and local object-to-background contrast are measuring different properties.</p>
 <p><strong>Area coverage and detector clipping quantify different properties.</strong> Only 0.0002% of Or98a GREEN export pixels reach 255 DN in each field, while median GREEN intensity is 39–41 DN. RED clipping is 0.0002–0.0003%. DAPI has substantial clipping and merged regions, but the reporter exports do not support calling Or98a “near-saturated.” Elevated local background is a possible contributor to lower object contrast.</p>
 <p>The <a href="measurement.html#area-versus-objects">measurement audit</a> details the difference between export clipping, broad background and segmentation.</p></section><section class="section-block" data-reveal="" id="supplementary"><h3 class="reading-heading--topic">Supplementary evidence</h3>
