 <p>All 420 supplied numeric baseline and excursion entries that could be compared match the independent reconstruction to the source’s four-decimal rounding. The audit also identifies two interpretation hazards: the supplied QC column labeled as a median contains first readings, and the supplied VUAA1 normalization uses a negative Or7a denominator, reversing signs. Transparent QC diagnostics replace undocumented ratios; VUAA1 normalization is omitted from the new figures.</p>
 <p>The source’s six retained untransfected corrected values reproduce SD = 0.04483 and 3 SD = 0.13448. These are heterogeneous single wells exposed to different additions, not a calibrated blank distribution. We do not use this value as a detection limit, a significance test or a positive/negative cutoff.</p>
